From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:46:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/23] rocket: rk3576: run MAX_POOL_2D on the PPU

Rocket only claimed convolutions and ADD on RK3576, so the max pools of
Inception and EfficientDet cut these models into many NPU/CPU partitions,
each costing a layout conversion and a submit.

Run MAX_POOL_2D (square kernels up to 5x5, the same quantization in and
out) as one PPU + PPU RDMA task, as the vendor compiler (rknn-toolkit2
2.3.2) emits it. rkt_ops.h reproduces the vendor's register streams for
the compiled cases apart from addresses and plane strides. The two-core
planner gives pooling all input rows and keeps it on core 0.

A PPU-only task raises the PPU interrupt instead of the DPU one, so
pooling is only claimed when the kernel reports
DRM_ROCKET_PARAM_PPU_TASKS; on older kernels it stays on the CPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
